# Polish letter-to-sound.
#
# One block a letter and its arms in order, the first that matches winning.
# The last arm of a block is the bare letter: what it says when nothing else
# applies. `before' is what must follow without being swallowed; an arm whose
# run is longer than its letter swallows the rest, which is how sz, cz, rz,
# dz, dż, dź and ch are one sound.
#
# A consonant before an i is the soft one, and the i is a softener rather than
# a vowel when a vowel follows it: Kasia is two syllables and dziś is one. So
# si before a vowel swallows the i, and s before an i leaves it to be spoken.
#
# A voiced consonant is voiceless before a voiceless one and at the end of a
# word -- raz is ras, babka is bapka, wtorek is ftorek -- and `voiceless'
# below counts both. w and rz also lose their voice after a voiceless one,
# which no other letter does: kwiat is kfiat and przy is pszy.
#
# Except that the end of a word is not voiceless when the next word begins
# with a voiced obstruent, which is `unless voiced follows': pod domem keeps
# its d. And there a voiceless one takes the voice, `before voiced word':
# jak dobrze is jag dobrze, kot biega is kod biega. w and rz do neither,
# being voiced without making what stands before them so -- brat wie keeps
# its t -- and so are not in `voiced'. A cluster at the end of a word takes
# the voice whole, so its arms swallow the rest of it: jest dobrze is jezd,
# and sześć złotych is szeźdź.
#
# Inside a word the same holds without the space, `before voiced': prośba
# is proźba, jakby jagby, liczba lidżba. A voiced letter counts only where it
# keeps its own voice, which is `unless voiceless follows' on its class, so
# liczb at the end of a word keeps its cz. And a voiced cluster loses its
# voice whole as well: gwiazd is gwiast, mózg músk.
#
# The phones are the engine's own, and several are named for the Italian
# sounds they took over, so the lines above the letters let an arm name them
# by Polish spelling instead. The vowels keep the engine's names, since e, o,
# y and c are phones already: e says E, the open ɛ; o says c, the open ɔ;
# y says e, the close-mid e Polish's ɨ took over; j says y, which is the
# engine's name for the glide; and ł says w, the other glide.
#
# f, p, t, v, k, x, a, l and m are still Italian's, copied from
# lang/itit/letters, and say what Italian's rules say, but for the arms
# above them that are Polish's: t before rz, and a voiceless final taking
# its voice from the next word.

rules in it_phone.obj named apply_pol_%s_rules
a piece runs from 864 to 872
a word runs from 704 to 712

voiceless means p t k f s c h ś ć sz cz and the end of the word unless voiced follows
voiced means b d g z ź ż unless voiceless follows
ą ć ę ł ń ś ź ż come through q

phone sz is L
phone ż is R
phone ś is S
phone ź is Z
phone ć is C
phone dź is J
phone dz is D
phone ń is N
phone ts is T
phone ch is A
phone ą is x
phone ę is o

letter s
  szcz before voiced word  says ż d ż  # deszcz go
  sz before voiced word  says ż     # nasz dom
  sz before voiced     says ż
  sz                   says sz      # szafa
  si before vowel      says ś       # Kasia
  s before i           says ś       # siła
  st before voiced word  says z d   # jest dobrze
  st before voiced     says z d     # natomiastbym
  s before voiced word says z       # las daleko
  s before voiced      says z
  s                    says s

letter c
  cz before voiced word  says d ż   # klucz do
  cz before voiced     says d ż     # liczba
  cz                   says t sz    # czas
  ch                   says ch      # chleb
  ci before vowel      says ć       # ciasto
  c before i           says ć       # cisza
  c before voiced word says dz      # noc była
  c before voiced      says dz
  c                    says ts      # cena

# rz is the voiced retroflex, not an r and a z. The words where it is one --
# marznie, and the others where the two letters meet across a seam in the
# word -- are the dictionary's to say.
letter r
  rz after voiceless   says sz      # przy, trzy, krzesło
  rz before voiceless  says sz      # tchórz
  rz                   says ż       # rzeka
  r                    says r

# dzi is asked about first, since the dz below would swallow it.
letter d
  dzi before vowel     says dź      # dziecko
  dz before i          says dź      # dzik
  dz before voiceless  says ts
  dz                   says dz      # dzwon
  dż before voiceless  says t sz
  dż                   says d ż     # dżem
  dź before voiceless  says ć
  dź                   says dź
  d before voiceless   says t       # kod
  d before rz          says d       marked tenseness tense   # drzewo
  d                    says d

letter z
  zau at word start    says z a u   # zaufanie, zauważyć
  zd before voiceless  says s t     # gwiazd, gwiazdka
  zg before voiceless  says s k     # mózg
  zi before vowel      says ź       # ziarno
  z before i           says ź       # zima
  z before voiceless   says s       # raz
  z                    says z

letter g
  g before voiceless   says k       # róg
  g                    says g

# The velar nasal before a k or a g is the phonology's, not the letter's:
# bank has it without being asked.
letter n
  nau at word start    says n a u   # nauka, nauczyciel
  nieu at word start   says ń E u   # nieufny, nieudany
  ni before vowel      says ń       # konie
  n before i           says ń       # nikt
  n                    says n

letter e
  e                    says E

letter o
  ó                    says u       # mój
  o                    says c

letter y
  y                    says e       # być

letter j
  j                    says y       # mój

letter b
  b before voiceless   says p       # chleb
  b                    says b

letter w
  w after voiceless    says f       # kwiat, twój, świat, czwartek
  w before voiceless   says f       # rów, wtorek
  w                    says v

letter h
  h                    says ch      # herbata

letter ą
  ą                    says ą

letter ę
  ę                    says ę

letter ł
  ł                    says w

letter ń
  ń                    says ń

letter ś
  ść before voiced word  says ź dź  # sześć złotych
  ś before voiced word says ź       # coś dobrego
  ś before voiced      says ź       # prośba
  ś                    says ś

letter ć
  ć before voiced word says dź      # być dobrym
  ć before voiced      says dź
  ć                    says ć

letter ź
  źdź before voiceless  says ś ć    # gwóźdź
  ź before voiceless   says ś
  ź                    says ź

letter ż
  ż before voiceless   says sz      # mąż
  ż                    says ż

letter f
  f before voiced word  says v     # szef banku
  f before voiced       says v
  ff   says f f   marked geminate yes
  f    says f

letter p
  p before voiced word  says b     # chłop go
  p before voiced       says b
  pp   says p p   marked geminate yes
  p    says p

# The t of trz and the d of drz end a cluster rather than start an affricate,
# and are marked so, `tense' being a value no consonant has and nothing else
# reads: the duration rules in is_dur.up give such a stop a longer release,
# which is what tells trzy from czy and drzewo from dżem.
letter t
  t before rz          says t       marked tenseness tense   # trzy
  tri before vowel at word start  says t r i   # trio, triumf, triangel
  t before voiced word  says d     # kot biega
  t before voiced       says d
  tt   says t t   marked geminate yes
  t    says t

letter v
  vv   says v v   marked geminate yes
  v    says v

letter k
  kt before voiced word  says g d  # fakt był
  k before voiced word  says g     # jak dobrze
  k before voiced       says g     # jakby, także
  k    says k

letter x
  x    says k s

letter a
  a    says a

letter l
  ll   says l l   marked geminate yes
  l    says l

letter m
  mm   says m m   marked geminate yes
  m    says m

# u is a vowel, Polish writing its glide ł. After a or e it is the glide,
# since au and eu are how Polish spells the diphthong of a loanword: auto,
# pauza, Europa, neutralny. Except where a word ends -eum or -eusz, muzeum and
# Mateusz, and where a prefix meets a u, which the n and z blocks take at the
# start of a word: nauka, zaufanie, nieufny.
letter u
  u accented             says u
  u after e before m at word end  says u   # muzeum, liceum
  u after e before sz at word end  says u  # Mateusz, Tadeusz
  u after a              says w     # auto, pauza, Australia
  u after e              says w     # Europa, neutralny
  u                      says u

letter i
  i accented             says i
  i after vowel          says i     # naiwny, moi
  i before vowel         says y     # biały, pies
  i                      says i
